\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Enriched backgrounds and comparison}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Which data must a comparison preserve for observables to survive?
The [finite background](fdip-000G), its reference pairing and retained
split already distinguish a relabeling from an arbitrary field map.
The [cycle trace ratio](fdip-000I) gives an observable with which to
test a proposed comparison.}

\p{The [enriched groupoid](fdip-000X) records allowed arrows and
the data they preserve. [Scalar invariants](fdip-000Y) descend
along those arrows without classifying all backgrounds.
[Quadratic isometry](fdip-000Z) can forget the reference pairing or
retained projection even while transporting a positive Gaussian law.
Its [Clifford functoriality](fdip-000Q) therefore need not retain all
the information required for these observables.}

\transclude{fdip-000X}
\transclude{fdip-000Y}
\transclude{fdip-000Z}
